 "profile": {
  "paragraphs": [
   "Reader Zone sells reading program software for teachers, schools, and public libraries, with program creation, reading progress tracking, and participation views in real time. For public libraries, the pages describe summer and year-round programs that are simple for patrons and practical for staff.",
   "For schools and districts, the product runs school-wide reading challenges and tracks participation across classrooms and groups from one place. For individual teachers, it runs classroom reading challenges without paper logs and shows who needs a nudge.",
   "Readers log books, minutes, pages, and activities through the app or web, and organizers track participation and reading progress from one dashboard. Readers join a program with a Program Code and log reading through the app or web. The about page states that the software works for any size and type of organization, from a single family to an entire school district or library system."
  ],
